From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: mesh: ignore beacons from other channels

ieee80211_mesh_rx_bcn_presp() derives the channel of a mesh beacon from
its DS Parameter Set element (or the RX frequency) and only checks that
the channel exists and is enabled. mesh_matches_local() does not compare
the primary channel either, except for 6 GHz peers that carry a 6 GHz
operation element.

Since a wiphy can have multiple radios, __ieee80211_rx_handle_packet()
passes management frames received by any radio to every interface. A
mesh interface on one radio therefore also processes the beacons of mesh
BSSes with the same mesh ID on the other radios' channels (e.g. the 5 GHz
mesh of a dual-band neighbour while this interface is on 6 GHz, or the
6 GHz beacons on a 5 GHz mesh). They match the local configuration, so
mesh_neighbour_update() creates a station or, with a user space MPM,
sends a new peer candidate event for a peer that cannot be reached on
this channel. The same applies to beacons received off-channel during a
scan and to 2.4 GHz beacons heard from an adjacent channel.

Ignore beacons and probe responses whose channel is not the operating
channel of the mesh interface.

The other mesh management frames have the same problem: a peer on
another radio's channel can still open a peering with a Mesh Peering
Open frame, which creates the station without any beacon, and probe
requests from other channels are answered. In
ieee80211_mesh_rx_queued_mgmt(), also ignore action frames and probe
requests whose RX frequency is not the frequency of the operating
channel. With a user space MPM the peering frames are not queued but
passed to user space from ieee80211_rx_h_action(), so drop them there
when they were received on another channel. Nothing is dropped while
the interface has no operating channel, and the frequency comparison
also covers 6 GHz, where frames carry no DS Parameter Set element.

Signed-off-by: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
---
 net/mac80211/mesh.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 net/mac80211/rx.c   | 12 +++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 35 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/mac80211/mesh.c b/net/mac80211/mesh.c
index 8f88141..b698fe2 100644
--- a/net/mac80211/mesh.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/mesh.c
@@ -1505,6 +1505,15 @@ static void ieee80211_mesh_rx_bcn_presp(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata,
 	if (!channel || channel->flags & IEEE80211_CHAN_DISABLED)
 		goto free;
 
+	/*
+	 * With multiple radios in one wiphy, frames received by any radio
+	 * are passed to all interfaces, so a mesh interface also sees the
+	 * beacons of mesh BSSes on the channels of the other radios. A
+	 * station on another channel cannot be a neighbour of this mesh.
+	 */
+	if (channel != sdata->vif.bss_conf.chanreq.oper.chan)
+		goto free;
+
 	if (mesh_matches_local(sdata, elems)) {
 		mpl_dbg(sdata, "rssi_threshold=%d,rx_status->signal=%d\n",
 			sdata->u.mesh.mshcfg.rssi_threshold, rx_status->signal);
@@ -1685,6 +1694,7 @@ void ieee80211_mesh_rx_queued_mgmt(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata,
 				   struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
 	struct ieee80211_rx_status *rx_status;
+	struct ieee80211_channel *chan;
 	struct ieee80211_mgmt *mgmt;
 	u16 stype;
 
@@ -1698,6 +1708,20 @@ void ieee80211_mesh_rx_queued_mgmt(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata,
 	mgmt = (struct ieee80211_mgmt *) skb->data;
 	stype = le16_to_cpu(mgmt->frame_control) & IEEE80211_FCTL_STYPE;
 
+	/*
+	 * With multiple radios in one wiphy, frames received by any radio
+	 * are passed to all interfaces. Peering and other action frames or
+	 * probe requests received on another channel come from stations
+	 * that cannot be neighbours of this mesh. Beacons and probe
+	 * responses are checked against the channel they advertise in
+	 * ieee80211_mesh_rx_bcn_presp().
+	 */
+	chan = sdata->vif.bss_conf.chanreq.oper.chan;
+	if ((stype == IEEE80211_STYPE_ACTION ||
+	     stype == IEEE80211_STYPE_PROBE_REQ) &&
+	    chan && chan->center_freq != rx_status->freq)
+		return;
+
 	switch (stype) {
 	case IEEE80211_STYPE_PROBE_RESP:
 	case IEEE80211_STYPE_BEACON:
diff --git a/net/mac80211/rx.c b/net/mac80211/rx.c
index d997504..975f720 100644
--- a/net/mac80211/rx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/rx.c
@@ -3861,9 +3861,19 @@ ieee80211_rx_h_action(struct ieee80211_rx_data *rx)
 		case WLAN_SP_MESH_PEERING_CONFIRM:
 			if (!ieee80211_vif_is_mesh(&sdata->vif))
 				goto invalid;
-			if (sdata->u.mesh.user_mpm)
+			if (sdata->u.mesh.user_mpm) {
+				struct ieee80211_channel *chan =
+					sdata->vif.bss_conf.chanreq.oper.chan;
+
+				/* With multiple radios in one wiphy, this
+				 * may come from another radio's channel;
+				 * see ieee80211_mesh_rx_queued_mgmt().
+				 */
+				if (chan && chan->center_freq != status->freq)
+					return RX_DROP_U_MESH_WRONG_ACTION;
 				/* userspace handles this frame */
 				break;
+			}
 			goto queue;
 		case WLAN_SP_MGK_INFORM:
 		case WLAN_SP_MGK_ACK:
